  "subject": "two strangers who each feed the same small stray dog on the riverside embankment at ten every night, each sure she is their dog and each calling her by a different name",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien indie soft-rock, a singer-songwriter band song. Clean Telecaster arpeggios with a light chorus effect; a Wurlitzer electric piano carrying the chords; warm round-wound electric bass; a live drum kit with brushes and cross-stick in the verses, switching to sticks and open hi-hat in the choruses; a thin string pad entering only in the last chorus. Dry and close, the vocal upfront and unreverbed, the band narrow behind it. Close-miked conversational female mezzo with little vibrato, restrained in the verses and double-tracked in the choruses. 92 BPM, A major. Shy, warm and getting braver. No reverb wash, no shoegaze haze, no fingerpicked folk guitar, no power-ballad build, no autotune, no trap drums.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n暗時十點 河邊的堤防\n我紮一个 狗仔罐頭\n彼隻花花的 細隻狗仔\n逐暗 佇路燈跤等我\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n今暝 伊食甲飽飽\n對面 徛一个提罐頭的人\n\n[Chorus]\n原來 毋是干焦我\n另外一个人 嘛共伊號名\n我叫伊麻糬 你叫伊阿花\n伊兩个名 攏應甲足好\n\n[Verse]\n第三暝 我刁工較早到\n你嘛 刁工較早到\n兩个人 坐佇堤防的兩爿\n麻糬 佇中央 毋知欲揀佗一爿\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n伊行來我遮 食一喙\n閣行去你遐 討一喙\n\n[Chorus]\n原來 毋是干焦我\n另外一个人 嘛共伊號名\n我叫伊麻糬 你叫伊阿花\n咱兩个 愈坐愈倚\n\n[Bridge]\n今暝落大雨 堤防干焦咱兩个\n麻糬 毋知覕佇佗位\n你喝阿花 我喝麻糬\n伊對你的雨幔內底 鑽出來\n\n[Chorus]\n原來 毋是干焦我\n另外一个人 嘛共伊號名\n叫麻糬嘛好 叫阿花嘛好\n伊有兩个名 咱有一隻狗\n\n[Outro]\n明仔暗 十點 堤防見\n罐頭紮一个 宵夜紮兩份",
